m92: draw each layer in one walk, skip tile rows with nothing to draw

Each M92 layer was drawn twice per line, once per priority pass, and every
pixel was tested against the pass mask and the screen edges. For every
layer and tile group the two pass masks are complementary, so each pixel
belongs to one pass only: both passes now go in one walk, each pixel with
its own pass priority. A table of the pens used by each 8x8 tile row
(built once at init) skips rows with nothing to draw. Same pixels written.

diff --git a/src/burn/drv/irem/d_m92.cpp b/src/burn/drv/irem/d_m92.cpp
--- a/src/burn/drv/irem/d_m92.cpp
